0,Armenia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armenia,"Armenia, officially the Republic of Armenia, is a landlocked country in the Armenian highlands of West Asia.Armenia is a member of the Council of Europe and maintains close relations with the European Union; especially with its member states France and Greece.","Armenian, Western",Indo-European
1,"Armenian language | History, Alphabet & Dialects | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/topic/Armenian-language,"Armenian language, language that forms a separate branch of the Indo-European language family; it was once erroneously considered a dialect of Iranian. In the early 21st century the Armenian language is spoken by some 6.7 million individuals.","Armenian, Western",Indo-European
2,Mobile Affixes Across Western Armenian: Conflicts Across Modules,https://www.academia.edu/41710126/Mobile_Affixes_Across_Western_Armenian_Conflicts_Across_Modules,"Verbs in Western Armenian (Indo-European) inflect for both subject agreement and tense. Subject and tense marking is often fused, which makes segmentation difficult.","Armenian, Western",Indo-European
3,(PDF) Armenian (Yerevan Eastern Armenian and Beirut Western...,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/374569268_Armenian_Yerevan_Eastern_Armenian_and_Beirut_Western_Armenian,"Verbs in Western Armenian (Indo-European) inflect for both subject agreement and tense. Subject and tense marking is often fused, which makes segmentation difficult. We show that, despite surface fusion, verbal inflection in Western Armenian is fundamentally agglutinative.","Armenian, Western",Indo-European
4,The Lone Wolf: Why Armenian is an Indo-European Mystery...,https://lingodigest.com/the-lone-wolf-why-armenian-is-an-indo-european-mystery/,"Every Indo-European language changes over time (which is why English father sounds different from Latin pater), but Armenian underwent a transformation that was particularly drastic. The most famous, almost notorious, example of this is the evolution of the number “two.”","Armenian, Western",Indo-European
5,Theme 2. the IND0-EUROPEAN language family. linguistic feature,https://oldenglish.at.ua/Presentations/Theme2.germaniclanguages.pdf,"INDO-EUROPEAN FAMILY. Centum group (''western'' languages)Indo-Iranian, Balto-Slavic (Baltic and. Slavic), Albanian, Armenian. lost the distinction between palatal velars and pure velars. [k,g,gh,kw,gw,gwh].","Armenian, Western",Indo-European
6,Indoeuropean music. Just like that! | Forum,https://www.theapricity.com/forum/showthread.php?344468-Indoeuropean-music-Just-like-that!,"I would appreciate, if music from asiatic branches would be typically recognizably indoeuropean and clearly normal, average (like in non Indo-Iranian branches). Maybe it can be hard to find, but I assume, it can be done.","Armenian, Western",Indo-European
7,"Armenian language lessons | Language lessons, Armenian language...",https://ca.pinterest.com/pin/armenian-language-lessons--92253492353714433/,"Armenian is an Indo-European language with about 6 million speakers mainly in Armenia [Hayastan] and Nagorno-Karabakh, a de facto, though unrecognised, independent republic in the Nagorno-Karabakh region of the South Caucasus.","Armenian, Western",Indo-European
